Decode the LZ4 (bv41) tracev3 chunks in the kernel KLOG dump (sweetloglz4=1).

0129 reads tracev3 files and scans them for printable strings, but the payload
chunks are LZ4-compressed, so it mostly sees file headers.  With
sweetloglz4=1 the KLOG path additionally walks each file for Apple's LZ4
stream markers and decompresses the blocks in the kernel with a small bounded
LZ4 block decoder, then runs the same printable-run + keyword filter on the
decompressed bytes and prints `KLOGD| <string>`.

Boot args (on top of the 0129 ones; default OFF = 0129 behaviour):
  sweetlogdump=1        enable the KLOG dump (0129)
  sweetloglz4=1         also decode bv41/bv4- tracev3 chunks (this patch)
  sweetlogtimes=...     as 0129 (default 240,420)
  sweetlogmax=...       as 0129 (cap on KLOG| lines)
  sweetlogdir=...       as 0129 (default .../diagnostics/Persist)

Tracev3 LZ4 framing (tmp/tracev3_format.asciidoc):
  bv41  u32 uncompressed_size  u32 compressed_size  <LZ4 block>
  bv4-  u32 uncompressed_size  <plaintext>
  bv4$  end of stream
Bounds: <=8 chunks/file, <=64 KiB decompressed output/chunk, <=512 KiB read
per file, <=200 KLOGD| lines per dump, malformed chunk => skipped.  For the
first 8 chunks a defensive line is printed so the framing can be checked
without another kernel build:

  KLOGZ chunk <n> magic=bv41 usize=<u> csize=<c> out=<o> err=<e>
  KLOGZ end chunks=<n> decoded=<n> bad=<n> bytes=<n> lines=<n>

Base: bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c after 0126, 0128 and 0129; only that file
changes.
